\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Out of the depths I cry to Thee,
\par Lord God. O hear my prayer!
\par Incline a gracious ear to me,
\par And bid me not despair:
\par If Thou rememberest each misdeed,
\par If each should have its rightful meed,
\par Lord, who shall stand before Thee?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. 'Tis through Thy love alone we gain
\par The pardon of our sin;
\par The strictest life is but in vain,
\par Our works can nothing win;
\par That none should boast himself of aught,
\par But own in fear Thy grace hath wrought
\par What in him seemeth righteous.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Wherefore my hope is in the Lord,
\par My works I count but dust,
\par I build not there, but on His word,
\par And in His goodness trust.
\par Up to His care myself I yield,
\par He is my tower, my rock, my shield,
\par And for His help I tarry.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And tough it linger till the night,
\par And round again till morn,
\par My heart shall ne'er mistrust Thy might,
\par Nor count itself forlorn.
\par Do thus, O ye of Israel's seed,
\par Ye of the Spirit born indeed,
\par Wait for your God's appearing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Though great our sins and sore our wounds,
\par And deep and dark our fall,
\par His helping mercy hath no bounds,
\par His love surpasseth all.
\par Our trusty loving Shepherd, He
\par Who shall at last set Israel free
\par From all their sin and sorrow.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

